# Cursor Rules Best Practices

## Rule Types

| Type | When Applied | Use Case |
|------|--------------|----------|
| Always Apply (`alwaysApply: true`) | Every chat | Core patterns, communication style |
| Agent-Decided (with `description`) | When relevant | Domain-specific patterns |
| File-Scoped (`globs`) | When files match | Feature-specific rules |
| Manual (`@rule-name`) | When mentioned | Specialized workflows |

## Rule File Structure
```markdown
---
description: Clear description for agent-decided rules
globs: pattern/**/*,*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Rule Title

Brief content focused on patterns and decisions.
Reference docs for full examples.
```

## Best Practices (from Cursor docs)

### Do ✅
- Keep rules under 500 lines
- Split large rules into composable parts
- Reference files instead of copying contents
- Provide concrete, actionable guidance
- Use globs for file-specific rules
- Write clear descriptions for agent-decided rules
- Check rules into git for team sharing

### Don't ❌
- Copy entire style guides (use linters)
- Document every CLI command (agent knows npm, git, etc.)
- Add edge case instructions that rarely apply
- Duplicate what's in your codebase
- Over-optimize before understanding patterns

## Rule Categories for This Project

**`AGENTS.md` is the canonical context source.** It is loaded every session by Cursor (and other agents) and holds behavioral rules, coding standards, monorepo structure, pattern complexity, and clean-architecture guidance. Per-app `AGENTS.md` files hold app-specific context. Do NOT duplicate that content here — `.cursor/rules` is only for Cursor-specific or on-demand reference material.

**Current rules (all on-demand, none always-applied):**
- `frontend-patterns.mdc` - Agent-decided. Complex-app code patterns (TanStack Query, hooks, server actions)
- `new-app-checklist.mdc` - Agent-decided/manual. Step-by-step new app onboarding template
- `cursor-rules.mdc` - File-scoped (`.cursor/rules/**`). This meta guide

**Add as needed:**
- App-specific context belongs in that app&apos;s `AGENTS.md`, not here
- Add a rule only for Cursor-specific behavior or detailed on-demand references that would bloat `AGENTS.md`

## Adding New Rules

1. Determine scope: always, agent-decided, file-scoped, or manual?
2. Write concise content (<100 lines ideal)
3. Reference existing docs for detailed examples
4. Add clear description for agent-decided rules
5. Use specific globs for file-scoped rules
6. Test by @-mentioning in chat to verify behavior
